<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91278" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτώξ</span></b> , ὁ, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτωκός, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτώσσω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cowering animal</i>, i.e.
				<i>hare</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.676
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				4.3.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				1.110
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτῶκα λαγωόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.310
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				102.10
			</span></i>: metaph. of a person, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				326
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Adj., <i>cowering</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτῶκα δ᾽ ἐν κλόνῳ δορός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					944
				</span></i>
			.</div>
